Honda Center","address":{"city":"Anaheim","state":"CA","zipCode":"92899","country":"USA"},"grass":false,"images":[{"href":"https://a.espncdn.com/i/venues/nhl/day/1842.jpg","width":2000,"height":1125,"alt":"","rel":["full","day"]}]},"attendance":17174,"officials":[{"fullName":"Tommy Hughes","displayName":"Tommy Hughes","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Chris Schlenker","displayName":"Chris Schlenker","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Michael Markovic","displayName":"Michael Markovic","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Travis Toomey","displayName":"Travis Toomey","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0}]},"article":{"headline":"Mikael Granlund scores in OT, Cutter Gauthier gets 2 goals in Ducks' 3-2 win over Panthers","description":"— Cutter Gauthier scored two power-play goals and captain Mikael Granlund had a power-play goal 4:14 into overtime, sending the Anaheim Ducks to a 3-2 victory over the Florida Panthers on Sunday night...","story":"ANAHEIM, Calif. -- — <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5080145/cutter-gauthier\">Cutter Gauthier</a> scored two power-play goals and captain <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5831/mikael-granlund\">Mikael Granlund</a> had a power-play goal 4:14 into overtime, sending the <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/anaheim-ducks\"><a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/ana/anaheim-ducks\">Anaheim Ducks</a></a> to a 3-2 victory over the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/fla/florida-panthers\">Florida Panthers</a> on Sunday night and their 11th consecutive win in home openers.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5149153/leo-carlsson\">Leo Carlsson</a> had three assists for the Ducks, including the setup for Granlund's winner in front of <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5452/jacob-markstrom\">Jacob Markstrom</a>.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4588165/lukas-dostal\">Lukas Dostal</a> made 29 saves for the Ducks, who have won their first two games following last season’s successful run to the second round of the playoffs, ending a seven-year postseason drought.\n\n\r\n              Gauthier delivered his 12th career multi-goal performance and added an assist on Granlund's winner in his first home game since he signed a six-year, $81 million contract extension last month coming off his 41-goal breakout season.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3852/brad-marchand\">Brad Marchand</a> tied it with 1:50 left in regulation in his season debut for the Panthers, who lost their second straight. <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3042088/carter-verhaeghe\">Carter Verhaeghe</a> scored an early goal and Markstrom stopped 18 shots.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5216858/beckett-sennecke\">Beckett Sennecke</a> drew a tripping penalty on <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3151784/gustav-forsling\">Gustav Forsling</a> midway through overtime, but Florida nearly killed the penalty before Carlsson found Granlund in front for his first goal. Carlsson has five points in his first two games after getting <a href=\"https://apnews.com/article/ducks-flyers-leo-carlsson-1aa92e7f1843fb05641d9f0b705ec22b\">his own $90 million extension</a>.\n\n\r\n              Gauthier scored from the slot on a power play early in the second off Sennecke's setup. Gauthier had an open net for a hat trick late in the second off another superb pass from Sennecke, but he hit the post — and snapped his stick over his knee in frustration moments later.\n\n\r\n              Florida failed to score on a late power play when former Panthers forward AJ Greer was sent off for hooking, but Marchand converted a rebound with Markstrom pulled for an extra attacker.\n\n\r\n              Defenseman <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3114717/aaron-ekblad\">Aaron Ekblad</a> was a late scratch for the Panthers, <a href=\"https://apnews.com/article/panthers-aleksander-barkov-injured-34633b257ec0dc0cbae92f42a27d5f13\">who lost captain <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3041970/aleksander-barkov\">Aleksander Barkov</a></a> to a significant left leg injury last Thursday.\n\n\r\n              Panthers defenseman <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5502/radko-gudas\">Radko Gudas</a> played against the team he captained for the previous two seasons, while Greer played against the team with which he spent the past two seasons, winning a Stanley Cup ring in 2025.\n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              Panthers: At Los Angeles on Tuesday night.\n\n\r\n              Ducks: Host Edmonton on Wednesday night.\n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              \r\n                <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/nhl\">See AP’s full NHL coverage here</a>","published":"2026-10-05T03:09:27Z"}}